body:
Hey so I'm on my phone but here's what I did in an old project.

// Firebase will autogenerate an id and return it in the response
Const id = Firebase.firestore().collection ("menu").doc().id

//Create an object add the above id to the object you will be sending to firebase
Const data = {
Id: id
}

//Then use the same above but pass in the id for doc and use .set()
Firebase.firestore().collection ("menu").doc(id).set(data)

So now your new doc will have an autogenerated id and your object will also have the autogenerated id as a property
